<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Porto-Novo</h1><p class="st-meta">1688 CE – 1908 CE (approx.) · capital Porto-Novo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Gun kingdom on the lagoon coast of Benin, rival of Dahomey, whose kings sought French protection and whose capital became the capital of French Dahomey.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tradition holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/te-agbanlin">Te Agbanlin</a>, a prince of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-allada">Kingdom of Allada</a>, founded the kingdom around 1688 at Hogbonu on the coastal lagoon, among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> communities who called it Ajashe. Portuguese traders named the place <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-novo">Porto-Novo</a>, and the kingdom grew as a port for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic trade</a>, often under pressure from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings, chosen in rotation among royal branches, ruled with ministers and nobles in a court shaped by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-allada">Allada</a> traditions and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> neighbours. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> was the mainstay until the mid-19th century, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palm-oil">palm oil</a> took over. The population mixed Gun, Yoruba and returning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agudas">Afro-Brazilians</a>, who brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and Brazilian-style architecture.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>King Soji accepted a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1863, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toffa-i">Toffa</a> renewed it in 1882 as protection against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-novo">Porto-Novo</a> became the capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-dahomey">French Dahomey</a>, and after Toffa's death in 1908 the French ended the monarchy's political role. It remains the official capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1688 CE – 1908 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.29%;width:4.38%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1688 CE – 1908 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Porto-Novo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Te Agbanlin, Soji, Toffa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vodun, with Islam and Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gun, Yoruba</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/benin">Benin</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Porto-Novo, Hogbonu, Ajashe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=kingdom-of-porto-novo" aria-label="Kingdom of Porto-Novo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4752 1935 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Porto-Novo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5072 2191L5109 2141M5072 2191L5054 728M5072 2191L5072 2192"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5109 2141h0M5054 728h0M5072 2192h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M